From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: mark the unused RF control override field on N-PHY rev 7+

The rev 7+ RF control override table has an entry for field 0x0800, which
drives PHY registers 0x07B and 0x07E, the RX gain 1 and 2 controls. No
code path in the driver ever passes that field.

An MMIO capture of the proprietary wl driver 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362 shows
it writing both registers during calibration, twelve times each. What b43
should do with them is not clear from the capture alone, since the driver
has no equivalent calibration to hang them off. Leave a marker so the next
person does not have to rediscover that the entry is dead.

Comment only.

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_nphy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_nphy.c
@@ -3206,6 +3206,7 @@
 	{ 0x0040, 0x07A, 0x07D, 0x0040, 6 },
 	{ 0x0080, 0x07A, 0x07D, 0x0080, 7 },
 	{ 0x0400, 0x0F8, 0x0FA, 0x0070, 4 },
+	/* TODO: unused field, the vendor writes 0x07B/0x07E during cal */
 	{ 0x0800, 0x07B, 0x07E, 0xFFFF, 0 },
 	{ 0x1000, 0x07C, 0x07F, 0xFFFF, 0 },
 	{ 0x6000, 0x348, 0x349, 0x00FF, 0 },

Note per il repo, non per la mailing list:

  - Registri: 0x07B = B43_NPHY_RFCTL_RXG1, 0x07E = RFCTL_RXG2.
  - Nella cattura: 12 scritture ciascuno, valori 0x0000 e 0x003c, prima
    occorrenza a #11769 e #12819, cioe' dentro la regione della calibrazione,
    intercalate a 0x343, 0x0e7, 0x342 che sono gli enable dell'override rev7.
  - Perche' solo un commento: la voce della tabella c'e' ed e' giusta, manca
    chi la usa, e chi la usa nel vendore e' una calibrazione che b43 non ha.
    Aggiungere una chiamata senza sapere in che fase e con che valori sarebbe
    inventare.
